<resources>
    <!-- NOTE the folder is values-iw, not values-he.
         Hebrew's ISO 639-1 code was changed from "iw" to "he" in 1989, but
         Java (and therefore Android) still normalises it back to the obsolete
         "iw" when resolving resources. A values-he folder is silently ignored:
         the locale applies - layout even flips to RTL - while every string
         quietly falls back to English, which looks like a translation bug
         rather than a folder-name one.

         app_name is deliberately absent: the brand stays "CalmSense" in Latin
         script, which is normal for software brands in Israel and avoids an
         awkward transliteration. Android falls back to values/strings.xml. -->

